{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20459",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 6.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Well, um, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.44,
      "end_seconds": 11.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Alright, that's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.35,
      "end_seconds": 15.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "It's pain in the finger, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.55,
      "end_seconds": 25.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.1,
      "end_seconds": 42.88,
      "duration_seconds": 16.78,
      "text": "Uh, honestly, a few times a day. A seven out of ten, I suppose. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.95,
      "end_seconds": 47.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.27,
      "end_seconds": 74.32,
      "duration_seconds": 25.05,
      "text": "Difficulty bending the finger goes along with it, most of the time. As for bleeding, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Okay, um, so the difficulty bending the finger? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.46,
      "end_seconds": 82.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Have you had pain in the finger before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.25,
      "end_seconds": 90.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Uh, a bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.05,
      "end_seconds": 103.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.49,
      "end_seconds": 111.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Nickel. I come out in... well, a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.42,
      "end_seconds": 115.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.68,
      "end_seconds": 128.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.26,
      "text": "I'm on Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. Sorry, what was I saying, I'm on propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.69,
      "end_seconds": 132.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.57,
      "end_seconds": 142.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Two months now. I'm on alendronate, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.41,
      "end_seconds": 145.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.25,
      "end_seconds": 147.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "It's 70 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.47,
      "end_seconds": 151.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "How long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.9,
      "end_seconds": 154.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "About a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.6,
      "end_seconds": 158.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.53,
      "end_seconds": 174.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.85,
      "text": "Hmm, I have asthma. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.12,
      "end_seconds": 178.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.51,
      "end_seconds": 188.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Migraines, for about ten years. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.65,
      "end_seconds": 190.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.93,
      "end_seconds": 195.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Hmm, I've had thin bones for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.77,
      "end_seconds": 204.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Alright, migraines, that matches what I have here. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.78,
      "end_seconds": 223.61,
      "duration_seconds": 17.83,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. Nothing, I'm teetotal. I hardly move around during the day. No, I share a house with my brother. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.42,
      "end_seconds": 227.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.02,
      "end_seconds": 236.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia. I mean, uh, my daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.58,
      "end_seconds": 244.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "A few quick ones: dirt in the wound, bite or weakness of the hand?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.7,
      "end_seconds": 250.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Ah, you know, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.84,
      "end_seconds": 254.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fever or pus?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.95,
      "end_seconds": 261.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.49,
      "end_seconds": 267.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "So, and redness spreading, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.52,
      "end_seconds": 271.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any redness spreading."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.63,
      "end_seconds": 275.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.9,
      "end_seconds": 278.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.46,
      "end_seconds": 283.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.86,
      "end_seconds": 285.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.19,
      "end_seconds": 307.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.87,
      "end_seconds": 317.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.54,
      "end_seconds": 346.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 98 percent on room air, BP is 117 over 72, pulse 72, temp 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.3,
      "end_seconds": 351.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.25,
      "end_seconds": 355.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.72,
      "end_seconds": 373.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.45,
      "end_seconds": 395.31,
      "duration_seconds": 19.86,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Okay, thinking it through, this is probably a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out an infected wound yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.48,
      "end_seconds": 398.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.71,
      "end_seconds": 418.81,
      "duration_seconds": 20.1,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury is my leading thought, not anything worse. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had pain in the finger, and no weakness of the hand or pus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.57,
      "end_seconds": 424.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "That's what happened, um, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.71,
      "end_seconds": 466.1,
      "duration_seconds": 26.39,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an X-ray of the finger because of laceration. Let's use tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day. It's for tetanus prevention. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 468.12,
      "end_seconds": 475.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "So, I take the tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 477.0,
      "end_seconds": 481.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 482.0,
      "end_seconds": 485.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 486.43,
      "end_seconds": 487.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}